One related case still leaves a stub: a fully qualified path, when the referencing file also has something else with that name (here an enum variant).

```rust
// a.rs
enum Msg {
    ChannelDsp(u32),
}

struct Pipeline {
    dsp: crate::b::ChannelDsp,
}

// b.rs
pub struct ChannelDsp {
    pub gain: f32,
}
```

`a_pipeline references channeldsp` lands on a node with no source file, even though the path names `b`. Without the `Msg::ChannelDsp` variant, the same reference resolves to `b_channeldsp` correctly. So it looks like the explicit `crate::b::` path isn't used to break the tie. Low priority on our side, just flagging it.

