> Recursive overridden member is reported as an affected hit via its own self-loop

Intended. A self-loop on `Base.m` is `Base.m` calling `m` on its own object, and for an `Impl` instance that call dispatches to `Impl.m`, so `Base.m` is a caller of the override, the same as a base overload calling the abstract member (the case the stepping-stone rule exists for: `JsonParser.getBinaryValue()` calling its own overload that `ParserBase` overrides, 124 such callers in jackson-core). Pinned in a27924fd: `test_recursive_overridden_member_is_a_caller_of_the_override` (`affected(Impl.m) == {Base.m: 1}`).

